   <text type="letter">
      
      <body>
         <div type="writingSession">
            <pb n="1"/>
            <opener><dateline>
                  <date when="1942-07-13">July 13, 1942</date></dateline><lb/>
               <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928" type="person">Professor Paul Tillich</rs><lb/>
               Union Theological Seminary<lb/> Broadway at 120th Street,<lb/>
               <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__319" type="place">New York, New York</rs>
               <salute>Dear <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928" type="person">Professor
                  Tillich</rs>:</salute>
            </opener>
            <p>It was very kind of you to interrupt your vacation long enough to send us your <rs ref="#L10581" type="letter">letter
               of July 10th</rs> about <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__75" type="person">Dr. Hannah Arendt-Bluecher</rs>. Your
            statement about her will be most helpful to us.</p>
            <p>I am not sure that we can assist her, but with your testimonial we shall certainly be
               prepared to speak about her in case opportunity offers.</p>
            <closer>
               <salute>Sincerely yours,</salute>
               <signed><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__492" type="person">Betty Drury</rs></signed><lb/>
               Executive Secretary </closer>
         </div>
      </body>
   </text>
